        "original_id": "263bfb75-777a-5f5d-925e-5d8814184d01",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Stein, Mary Alice Stephenson, VJ Logan, Charles Russell, Bob Engelman, Mike Werb\n- Works: Ferris Bueller's Day Off, The Mask, Son of the Mask, America's Most Smartest Model\n- Organizations: Dark Horse Comics\n- Roles: host, winner, director, producer, writer, actor, model\n\nFacts:\n- Ben Stein is best known on screen as the economics teacher in \"Ferris Bueller's Day Off\" (1986).\n- VJ Logan, born Van Jameson Lingenfelter Logan in 1986, is an American model.\n- Ben Stein played Dr. Arthur Neuman in \"The Mask\" (1994).\n- \"The Mask\" is a 1994 American superhero fantasy comedy film directed by Charles Russell, produced by Bob Engelman, and written by Mike Werb.\n- \"The Mask\" was based on the comic series of the same name distributed by Dark Horse Comics.\n- Ben Stein played Dr. Arthur Neuman again in \"Son of the Mask\" (2005).\n- \"America's Most Smartest Model\" was hosted by Ben Stein and Mary Alice Stephenson.\n- VJ Logan is best known for winning the reality competition television program \"America's Most Smartest Model\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cccdc636-2bb5-5da9-b1f7-57c121437db2",
        "text": "Page: Ben Stein. Sentence: He is most well-known on screen as the economics teacher in \"Ferris Bueller's Day Off\" (1986) and as Dr. Arthur Neuman in \"The Mask\" (1994) and \"Son of the Mask\" (2005).\nPage: The Mask (film). Sentence: The Mask is a 1994 American superhero fantasy comedy film directed by Charles Russell, produced by Bob Engelman, and written by Mike Werb, based on the comic series of the same name distributed by Dark Horse Comics.\nPage: America's Most Smartest Model. Sentence: The hosts were Ben Stein and Mary Alice Stephenson.\nPage: VJ Logan. Sentence: Van Jameson Lingenfelter Logan, better known under the stage name of VJ Logan (born in 1986), is an American model who is best known for being the winner of the reality competition television program \"America's Most Smartest Model\".",
